### Option (a): Bookshop 5-Digit Barcode Check-Digit Program (150 Books)

**GW-BASIC Program (2018 Exam):**
```basic
10 CLS
20 FOR B = 1 TO 150
30 INPUT "Enter 1st, 2nd, 3rd, and 4th digits of barcode: "; D1, D2, D3, D4
40 LET S1 = (D1 + D3) * 3
50 LET S2 = D2 + D4
60 LET S3 = S1 + S2
70 LET REMVAL = S3 MOD 10
80 IF REMVAL = 0 THEN CD = 0 ELSE CD = 10 - REMVAL
90 PRINT "Check digit for book "; B; " is: "; CD
100 NEXT B
110 END
```

**2025 Syllabus Equivalent (JavaScript):**
```javascript
for (let b = 1; b <= 150; b++) {
    let d1 = parseInt(prompt("Book " + b + " - Enter 1st digit:"));
    let d2 = parseInt(prompt("Book " + b + " - Enter 2nd digit:"));
    let d3 = parseInt(prompt("Book " + b + " - Enter 3rd digit:"));
    let d4 = parseInt(prompt("Book " + b + " - Enter 4th digit:"));
    let s1 = (d1 + d3) * 3;
    let s2 = d2 + d4;
    let rem = (s1 + s2) % 10;
    let checkDigit = (rem === 0) ? 0 : (10 - rem);
    document.write("Book " + b + " Check Digit: " + checkDigit + "<br>");
}
```

### Option (b): Element-Wise Addition of Two 15-Element 1D Arrays (`C = A + B`)

**GW-BASIC Program (2018 Exam):**
```basic
10 CLS
20 DIM A(15), B(15), C(15)
30 FOR T = 1 TO 15
40 INPUT "Enter value for Array A: "; A(T)
50 INPUT "Enter value for Array B: "; B(T)
60 C(T) = A(T) + B(T)
70 NEXT T
80 FOR T = 1 TO 15
90 PRINT "Sum at position "; T; " = "; C(T)
100 NEXT T
110 END
```

**2025 Syllabus Equivalent (JavaScript):**
```javascript
let A = new Array(15);
let B = new Array(15);
let C = new Array(15);
for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) {
    A[i] = parseInt(prompt("Enter element " + (i + 1) + " for Array A:"));
    B[i] = parseInt(prompt("Enter element " + (i + 1) + " for Array B:"));
    C[i] = A[i] + B[i];
    document.write("C[" + i + "] = " + C[i] + "<br>");
}
```
